            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for a journey, then the Hindi for luggage."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: नक़्शा",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "नक़्शा — naqśā — \"a map\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "नक़्शा (naqśā) is a loan from Arabic naqsh, \"a painting, an engraving\", which reached Hindi through Persian. Its Arabic root is n-q-sh (Lane). Hindi naqśā came through Persian naqsha, \"a drawing, a plan\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
